course: dictionary
lesson: 12853
title: Enforceable: rules that can be checked
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A rule is enforceable when it can really be made to happen. People can be made to obey it, and there is a way to punish or stop those who break it. Enforceable is an adjective, so it describes a rule, law or agreement.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «The school rule that phones must stay in bags is enforceable, because teachers can take a phone away if someone breaks it.» The words teachers can take a phone away show that the rule can be checked and backed up.
explain: Compare that with «Be nicer to each other.» That sounds good, but how would anyone check it or make it happen? It is not enforceable. A good test is to ask: can someone actually make this happen, and is there a way to deal with people who break it?
explain: In law, a contract is enforceable if a court will make the people in it keep their promises. So enforceable is about whether a rule or promise has real backing behind it.
fact: Enforceable means that a rule, law or agreement can really be made to happen.
fact: «The new law is enforceable, so the council can fine people who break it.» Here enforceable means the council has a way to make people obey it.
fact: «A contract is enforceable if a court will make the people in it keep their promises.»
fact: A rule that nobody can check or back up is not enforceable.
fact: Its forms are enforceable, more enforceable and most enforceable.
exercise: «The rule that everyone must wear a seatbelt is enforceable.» What does enforceable mean here? | *It can be made to happen, and people can be stopped or punished if they break it | It is very old | It is written in red ink | It is a very long rule
exercise: Which rule is enforceable? | Try your best | Everyone should feel happy | *No phones in class, and a phone is taken away if it is used | Be kind to everyone at all times
exercise: «A contract is enforceable if a court will make the people in it keep their promises.» What does this tell you? | The people must become friends | The court will forget the promises | The contract is written in pencil | *A court can make the people keep their promises
test: A rule that nobody can check or back up is | More enforceable than most | A very enforceable rule | *Not enforceable
test: «Be nicer to each other» is hard to enforce, so why is it not enforceable? | Because it is a law | Because it is too short | Because it is written in blue ink | *Because nobody can check it or make it happen
exam: Ruby says, «Our club rules are only wishes, not enforceable.» What does she mean? | The club has too many members | The rules are very old | *The rules cannot be made to happen or checked, so nobody can be stopped if they break them | The rules are sung every Friday
